Intercom first desktop voice and context-mesh slice

Workstream ID: ic-06
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Intercom/issues/5
Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: One observable voice-to-existing-session-to-spoken-result loop
Dependencies: ic-02, ic-04, ic-05

Purpose:
  Implement the bounded desktop experience only after separate authorization
  and qualification. Electron/React/Three.js remains a stack recommendation.

Tasks:
  [ ] Obtain implementation authority and finalize stack/dependency choices.
  [ ] Build an isolated desktop host, audio controls and selected speech pipeline.
  [ ] Add selectable priorities with Speed/performance default and saved choice.
  [ ] Route finalized utterances with explicit context/session identity.
  [ ] Implement terminal handoff and approved background dispatch.
  [ ] Render a spherical mesh with observed activity and unknown-coverage states.
  [ ] Persist job outcomes and deliver accurate notifications/spoken summaries.
  [ ] Cover ambiguity, permission, failure, cancellation and accessible fallback.
  [ ] Document actual build/test/launch commands and remaining evidence limits.

Acceptance criteria:
  The docs/roadmap.md first-slice scenario passes on disposable test data.
  Voice remains available while a request runs without model-based status polling.
  No fabricated reads, false completion, unrestricted tools or duplicate dispatch.
  Playback interruption is separate from task cancellation.
  Proposed runtime isolation is demonstrated, not inferred from different paths.
  Human voice/visual acceptance is recorded separately from automated checks.
  Profile changes apply at a request boundary without changing running jobs,
  permissions or approved providers; default performance meets agreed budgets.

Completion evidence:
  None. No application, dependency manifest, runtime, preview or installer exists.

Completion log:
  2026-11-10 - Recorded as gated future work, not authorized implementation.
